        "original_id": "dd75f146-db22-50d0-9840-4c69813dae70",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals: Beaver and Erie Canal, Erie Extension Canal, Dismal Swamp Canal\n- Systems: Pennsylvania Canal system\n- Canal divisions: Beaver Division, Shenango Division, Conneaut Division\n- Places: Great Dismal Swamp, Virginia, North Carolina, United States\n- Buildings and services: Nicholson House and Inn, stagecoach stop, inn, post office, farm supply store, general store, trolley stop\n- Transit lines: Buffalo and Conneaut trolley line\n\nFacts:\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal, also known as the Erie Extension Canal, was part of the Pennsylvania Canal system.\n- The Beaver and Erie Canal consisted of the Beaver Division, the Shenango Division, and the Conneaut Division.\n- The Dismal Swamp Canal is located along the eastern edge of the Great Dismal Swamp in Virginia and North Carolina in the United States.\n- From 1842 to 1857, the Nicholson House and Inn served as a post office.\n- The Nicholson House and Inn served as a stagecoach stop, an inn along the Erie Extension Canal, a farm supply and general store, and a stop on the Buffalo and Conneaut trolley line.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
